A2. Univariate feature scan
For every candidate feature column (all columns except identifiers, split, and the four outcome columns — see data card):

type (numeric vs categorical);
missingness count and %;
for numeric: mean, std, min, max (on train);
for categorical: number of levels and top 5 levels (on train).

Present as a compact table printed out in your notebook.

B2. Model choice
Choose one simple model you can train, for example:

logistic regression;
a tree-based model;
a method from DATA 322;
another method you can justify.

State input features (subset of columns), how you encode categoricals, and how you handle missing values (rules fit on train only).
